 the syncState method to only apply aria-hidden when the menu button is visible (i.e., in mobile/viewport where the navigation is hidden via CSS), preserving the default accessible state on desktop.","edits":[{"path":"src/govuk/components/header/header.js","sha256":"33e331b7a1f44087522e90d1e295dbc0f915c8b8a82e8afd57a794d21fff4424","before":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', !isVisible)\n}","after":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  // Only manage aria-hidden when menu button is visible (mobile)\n  if (this.$menuButton.offsetWidth || this.$menuButton.offsetHeight) {\n    this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', !isVisible)\n  }\n}"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Navigation links will be exposed as links in the accessibility tree, enabling screen reader and keyboard users to discover and activate them.","functional_risks":["If the visibility check fails, the navigation could remain hidden from assistive technology on mobile when opened, or remain visible on desktop when it should be hidden. The check uses offsetWidth/offsetHeight which reliably reflects the button's CSS display state."],"verification_requirements":["After the fix, the ax assertion for the 'Apply' link must pass (role link, name 'Apply').","When the menu button is clicked in a narrow viewport, the navigation's aria-hidden attribute should toggle between true (closed) and false (open).","Ensure no regression in the visual presentation of the header across breakpoints."]},"provenance":{"provider":"Nebius Token Factory","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","requestId":"chatcmpl-8aba4a1d794c24198e898494b72679bf","promptHash":"8d65dd017